meta {
  name: 1 List professions (anonymous)
  type: http
  seq: 1
}
get {
  url: {{professionUrl}}/api/v1/professions
  auth: none
}
tests {
  test("200 WITHOUT a token — this must stay anonymous", function () {
    expect(res.getStatus()).to.equal(200);
  });
}
docs {
  **Deliberately still anonymous** (AC-18). Reference data seeded from `ProfessionSeedData.cs`, no PII —
  so F-016 left it open on purpose. A blanket "authenticate all the GETs" change is the obvious way to
  break this, which is why there is a test asserting it.

  `auth: none` here overrides the collection bearer token, proving it works unauthenticated.
}
